course: dictionary
lesson: 9300
title: Specialist words in context
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: A specialist is a person who knows a great deal about one subject, or who does one kind of work very well. Context helps you find this. «In the UK your first stop for most health problems is the GP, who knows a little about everything and sends you to a specialist when needed.» A GP knows a little about everything, so a specialist must know one thing very deeply.
explain: «Play specialists use dolls, pictures and games to show children what will happen.» Play specialists do one kind of work: helping children with play. Check your meaning by swapping it in: "Play experts use dolls, pictures and games to show children what will happen." It still makes sense, so your meaning is right.
explain: Specialist can also be an adjective, which describes a thing. «Specialist equipment» is equipment for one particular purpose or for experts. «Children's wards have nurses, doctors and play specialists» shows that specialists are people who work in one special area of a hospital.
fact: Specialist can be a noun (a specialist) or an adjective (specialist).
fact: A specialist is a person who knows a lot about one subject or does one kind of work very well.
fact: In health, a specialist is a doctor who treats one part of the body or one kind of illness, like a heart specialist.
fact: As an adjective, «specialist» means for one particular purpose or for experts, as in «specialist equipment».
fact: Useful phrases: «a specialist in», «see a specialist», «specialist knowledge».
exercise: «In the UK your first stop is the GP, who knows a little about everything.» What does a specialist know? | *One subject or one kind of work very well | Nothing at all about health | How to drive a bus | Everything about every subject
exercise: «Play specialists use dolls, pictures and games to show children what will happen.» What do play specialists use? | *Dolls, pictures and games | Cars and bikes | Needles and bandages | Rulers and pencils
exercise: «Specialist equipment» is equipment that is for | eating dinner | breaking things | everyone, for every job | *one particular purpose
test: A heart specialist is a doctor who treats which part of the body? | *Heart | Feet | Head | Ears
test: «See a specialist» most likely means | stop reading the book | sing a song loudly | go to the shops for food | *go to an expert who knows one area very well
exam: Jayden says a specialist is a teacher who teaches everything. Why is he wrong? | A specialist is always a doctor in a hospital | Specialists never work with children | Specialists are only nurses | *A specialist knows one subject or kind of work deeply, not everything
